/*****************************************************************************
    jitXcall -- ACTION-INVOKES-ANOTHER-ACTION UNDER JIT. 2026-08-08.

    THE MEASUREMENT THE genKantParse BRIEF ASKS FOR (Clod's item 4). Every
    other call rung measures a call to a purpose-built C++ extern through the
    fallback column (jitTrace/jitEmitTrace at J6, displayFill at the forms
    seam) or a SELF-call through jitEmitSelfCall (JR). NOTHING MEASURES ONE
    KANT ACTION CALLING A DIFFERENT KANT ACTION -- which is exactly what
    genKantParse's most common plan node, CALL (`t1()`), compiles to.

    THE CLAIM UNDER TEST: `jxCallee();` inside a jitted body is EMITTED and
    runs at RUN time, once per fire.

    THE RIVAL, and it is what aCTionRunRulE's source predicts: that handler
    carries NO `if jitting` gate and NO jitDegrade call, so under jitting the
    callee is simply INTERPRETED during the emit walk and nothing is emitted.
    That failure is SILENT and reports degrade count 0.

    jxTicks is the discriminator and it is a COUNT, not an absence (H4): the
    callee bumps it on every entry, so the number distinguishes the readings
    rather than a missing line doing it.

    DIAGNOSTIC:
        fire1 out=8  fire2 out=22  ticks=2   EMITTED, runs at run time
        fire1 out=8  fire2 out=8   ticks=1   ran at EMIT time, nothing emitted
        fire1 out=0  fire2 out=0   ticks=0   the call never happened at all

    Fire 2 changes the input AFTER emission with no recompile, so 8-then-22 can
    only come from compiled code re-reading the field.

    ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING (bear-trap #25): the jitted half FIRST, because
    testing() routes on isCoded and an interpreted run consumes it. The oracle
    is last.

    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (H2).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitXcall);
define
    jxIn;
    jxOut;
    jxTicks;
    jxCallee code={
        jxTicks = jxTicks + 1;
        jxOut = jxIn * 2;
        };
    jxDriver code={
        jxCallee();
        };
    ;

jxIn    = 4;
jxOut   = 0;
jxTicks = 0;
print "XC fire 1 setup : jxIn =" jxIn:;
testing(jxDriver);
print "XC fire 1 result: jxOut =" jxOut " (want 8)  jxTicks =" jxTicks:;

jxIn  = 11;
jxOut = 0;
print "XC fire 2 setup : jxIn =" jxIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "XC fire 2 result: jxOut =" jxOut " (want 22) jxTicks =" jxTicks:;

print "XC TICKS TOTAL  : jxTicks =" jxTicks " (want 2 -- emitted; 1 means emit-time)":;

jxIn    = 4;
jxOut   = 0;
jxTicks = 0;
jxDriver();
print "XC interpreted  : jxOut =" jxOut " (the oracle -- want 8) jxTicks =" jxTicks:;

print "XC SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
